SELECT 'forged-land-documents-ghana-red-flags', 'Forged Land Documents in Ghana: 7 Red Flags Before You Pay', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Forged Ghana land documents share seven tells: no GRA stamp duty stamp, site plan mismatched to the indenture, missing solicitor seal, no traceable Lands Commission number, ''freehold for foreigners'' claims, personal-account payment routing, and urgency. Verify all seven before any significant payment.</p><h2>What do forged documents look like?</h2><p>Convincing - visually. Forgers copy legitimate indentures and site plans but skip the parts that cost money or leave trails: <strong>stamp duty (0.25-1% via GRA)</strong>, solicitor certification, and actual registration. The document looks right; the registry has never seen it.</p><h2>What are the 7 red flags?</h2><p><strong>1. No stamp duty stamp.</strong> Genuine instruments carry GRA stamps. <strong>2. Site plan mismatch</strong> - owner name, size or location differs from the indenture. <strong>3. Missing solicitor seal.</strong> <strong>4. No traceable registration number</strong> at the Lands Commission. <strong>5. ''Freehold'' offered to a foreigner</strong> - legally impossible; foreigners cap at 50-year leasehold. <strong>6. Payment to personal accounts</strong> instead of lawyer escrow. <strong>7. Urgency pressure</strong> - ''pay today, verify later''.</p><h2>How do you verify each document?</h2><p>Run the <strong>Lands Commission search (GHS 400)</strong> and demand the search report; cross-check indenture vs site plan vs seller ID in person; confirm stamp duty receipts with GRA; have your own lawyer - not the seller''s - certify everything. One failed check stops the deal.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Forgery is visual; verification is bureaucratic - do the boring checks.</li><li>A document without a registry trace is decoration, not title.</li><li>Your lawyer verifies; the seller''s lawyer sells.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Can I verify documents remotely?</strong><br>Partially via the Lands Commission online portal, but confirm through your lawyer''s physical search - portal coverage is still expanding by region.</p><p><strong>What does verification cost?</strong><br>Search GHS 400, legal 1-2% of price, registration ~1-2% - total closing 2-4%. Fraud costs 100%.</p><p><strong>Are old colonial-era documents valid?</strong><br>Only if the chain to a registered title holds. Age adds prestige, not proof - verify identically.</p><p><em>Sources: The Africanvestor 2026; Ownkey 2026; Land Act 2020.</em></p><p><em>Buying land in Ghana? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> maps verified diaspora lawyers, surveyors and REAC-registered agents - diligence before deposits.</em></p>', 'Fake indentures, cloned site plans, missing stamp duty. The 7 document red flags that expose forged Ghana land papers - and how to verify each one.', ARRAY['land','fraud','documents','indenture','verification'], 'Land & Title', 'published', '2026-10-09T08:00:00.000Z', 'Forged Land Documents in Ghana: 7 Red Flags', 'Fake indentures and cloned site plans: 7 red flags in Ghana land documents and exactly how to verify each one before paying.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'forged-land-documents-ghana-red-flags');
