SELECT 'fake-power-of-attorney-ghana-land-scams', 'Fake Power of Attorney Land Scams in Ghana (and Real POA Done Right)', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> The commonest impersonation scam: someone claims to sell as the owner''s representative via a forged power of attorney. Defense: verify the representative''s authority directly with the registered owner, and use a properly consularized POA (notarised abroad + Ghana mission endorsement) for your own remote purchases.</p><h2>How does the fake-POA scam work?</h2><p>A ''nephew'', ''caretaker'' or ''family head'' presents land with documents that look legitimate, collects your deposit, and vanishes - or the real owner surfaces later having never authorised the sale. Remote diaspora buyers who never meet the registered owner are the standard victims.</p><h2>How do you check a representative''s authority?</h2><p><strong>Speak to the registered owner yourself</strong> - video call with ID matched to the title. Confirm the POA''s scope, dates and signatures with your lawyer. Cross-check at the Lands Commission that no competing representative claims exist. Never accept ''the owner is unreachable'' as an answer.</p><h2>How do you set up a REAL POA from abroad?</h2><p>1. Draft with your Ghana lawyer - <strong>exact scope, named parties, monetary limits, duration</strong>. 2. Sign before a notary in your country. 3. <strong>Consularize at the Ghana High Commission/Embassy</strong> - Ghana is not in the Hague Apostille Convention, so apostille alone fails. 4. Your lawyer then signs, pays and registers in your name.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Their POA: verify with the owner directly or walk away.</li><li>Your POA: narrow scope, capped amounts, fixed duration.</li><li>Broad, open-ended POAs are the #2 abuse vector after multiple-sale.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Can family members sell on my behalf safely?</strong><br>Only under a scoped, consularized POA with independent lawyer oversight - ''trust me, I''m family'' is how most diaspora losses begin.</p><p><strong>How long does consularization take?</strong><br>Days to weeks depending on the mission; start it before you agree prices, not after.</p><p><strong>Can I revoke a POA?</strong><br>Yes - in writing, notified to all parties and the Lands Commission. Revoke the moment its job is done.</p><p><em>Sources: MyJoyOnline buying guide 2026; Firmus Advisory land series.</em></p><p><em>Buying land in Ghana? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> maps verified diaspora lawyers, surveyors and REAC-registered agents - diligence before deposits.</em></p>', '''Uncle'' sells family land with a POA nobody signed. How fake representative scams work, and the consularized-POA process that protects remote buyers.', ARRAY['land','fraud','power of attorney','diaspora'], 'Land & Title', 'published', '2026-10-09T08:00:00.000Z', 'Fake Power of Attorney Land Scams in Ghana', 'Fake POAs and ''family reps'' drive Ghana land scams. How the con works plus the consularized-POA process that protects remote diaspora buyers.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'fake-power-of-attorney-ghana-land-scams');
