SELECT 'land-guards-ghana-law-protection-guide', 'Land Guards in Ghana: What the Law Says and How Buyers Stay Safe', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> The Land Act 2020 criminalises land-guard activity (5-15 years imprisonment), but enforcement is uneven - especially on unregistered peri-urban plots. Prevention: registered title, fenced boundaries, visible caretaker, documented customary consent. Never engage directly; report to police + lawyer.</p><h2>Who are land guards and where do they operate?</h2><p>Armed groups who appear after purchase claiming traditional ownership, demanding payments or evicting buyers. Hotspots: <strong>peri-urban Accra and Kumasi</strong> where customary boundaries are contested. Informal family-head purchases without verified authority are the standard trigger.</p><h2>What does the law actually do?</h2><p>Act 1036 (2020) makes land-guard deployment a serious crime: <strong>5-15 years imprisonment</strong>, plus the Real Estate Agency Act regulates agents. The framework is strong; the gap is enforcement bandwidth and the years cases take. Your safety cannot depend on prosecution speed.</p><h2>What is the buyer prevention protocol?</h2><p>1. <strong>Register immediately</strong> after purchase. 2. <strong>Fence + signage + caretaker</strong> visible to the community. 3. <strong>Customary consent documented</strong> alongside registration. 4. Build community ties early (assembly member, neighbours). 5. If approached: <strong>disengage, document, report</strong> - Police Property Fraud Unit + your lawyer, same day.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Land guards harvest unregistered, unfenced, absentee plots.</li><li>The law punishes; only your title + presence protects.</li><li>Never pay ''settlement'' - it marks you as a revenue stream.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Should I hire my own guards?</strong><br>A licensed caretaker/security firm, yes. Freelance ''protection'', no - it feeds the same economy.</p><p><strong>Are estates safer?</strong><br>Yes - registered developments with management rarely face guard issues. Another absentee-buyer argument for estates.</p><p><strong>What evidence helps police?</strong><br>Registered title, dated photos, caretaker logs, payment records - paper first, always.</p><p><em>Sources: Land Act 2020 (Act 1036); Ownkey fraud guide 2026; Ghana Police Property Fraud Unit.</em></p><p><em>Buying land in Ghana? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> maps verified diaspora lawyers, surveyors and REAC-registered agents - diligence before deposits.</em></p>', 'Armed men at your plot demanding ''settlement''? The Land Act''s 5-15 year penalties, why enforcement lags, and the buyer protocol that prevents encounters.', ARRAY['land','land guards','security','law'], 'Land & Title', 'published', '2026-10-09T08:00:00.000Z', 'Land Guards in Ghana: Law & Buyer Safety', 'Land guards, the law''s 5-15 year penalties, and the buyer protocol - register, fence, caretaker - that keeps you from ever meeting them.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'land-guards-ghana-law-protection-guide');
