SELECT 'can-foreigners-own-land-ghana-50-year-rule', 'Can Foreigners Own Land in Ghana? The 50-Year Leasehold Rule Explained', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Foreigners (including naturalised diasporans without Ghanaian citizenship) can only hold <strong>leasehold interests of max 50 years per grant</strong> (Constitution Art. 266 + Land Act 2020) - no freehold, no automatic renewal unless contracted. Ghanaian citizens access 99-year renewable leaseholds. Both structures allow occupying, renting, selling the lease, and inheritance within term.</p><h2>What exactly can a foreigner hold?</h2><p>A leasehold: exclusive possession for a fixed term. Within term you can live there, rent it out (15% non-resident rental tax), sell/assign the remainder, mortgage it, and pass it on. What you cannot do: hold freehold, or exceed 50 years in one grant. A seller offering ''60 years'' or ''freehold to foreigners'' is misrepresenting the law.</p><h2>What must the agreement contain?</h2><p><strong>Express renewal clause</strong> (foreigners have no automatic renewal - citizens do), ground-rent terms, consent-to-assign provisions, and dispute forum. Renewal negotiation happens from strength only if contracted upfront.</p><h2>What about dual citizens?</h2><p>Ghanaian citizenship (including dual) unlocks the <strong>99-year renewable</strong> citizen track with full rights. This alone justifies pursuing Right of Abode/citizenship early for serious investors.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>50 years per grant, renewal only if written in.</li><li>Leasehold still builds wealth: Carrefour, Diageo and every major operator lease.</li><li>''Freehold for foreigners'' = instant scam verdict.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Can I renew after 50 years?</strong><br>Yes if your agreement provides for it - negotiate renewal terms, rent reviews and who pays registration before signing, not in year 49.</p><p><strong>Can foreigners buy apartments?</strong><br>Yes - units in registered developments on the same leasehold basis; the cleanest entry for remote buyers.</p><p><strong>Does marriage to a Ghanaian change this?</strong><br>Not automatically - title follows the holder''s citizenship status. Structure deliberately with counsel.</p><p><em>Sources: 1992 Constitution Art. 266; Land Act 2020; Firmus Advisory.</em></p><p><em>Buying land in Ghana? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> maps verified diaspora lawyers, surveyors and REAC-registered agents - diligence before deposits.</em></p>', 'No freehold for non-citizens, 50 years max per grant, no automatic renewal. The exact legal structure - plus the 99-year path for Ghanaian citizens.', ARRAY['land','leasehold','foreigners','law','Article 266'], 'Land & Title', 'published', '2026-10-09T08:00:00.000Z', 'Can Foreigners Own Land in Ghana? 50-Year Rule', 'No freehold for foreigners: Ghana''s 50-year leasehold cap explained, renewal clauses that matter, and the 99-year citizen path.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'can-foreigners-own-land-ghana-50-year-rule');
