SELECT 'lands-commission-title-search-ghana-walkthrough', 'Lands Commission Title Search in Ghana: The GHS 400 Walkthrough', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Before paying any significant money, run a Lands Commission search (GHS 400): it reveals the registered owner, plot dimensions/boundaries, and competing claims or encumbrances. Do it via your lawyer in person plus the online portal; proceed only on a clean report.</p><h2>What does the search actually reveal?</h2><p>Three things that decide everything: <strong>who is registered</strong> (match to the seller''s ID), <strong>what exactly</strong> (dimensions, boundaries, site-plan alignment), and <strong>what''s burdening it</strong> (competing claims, charges, stool/state interests, zoning flags). A clean report is the only green light that matters.</p><h2>How do you run it step by step?</h2><p>1. Your lawyer submits the indenture/site-plan copies + fee. 2. Registry officials trace the chain. 3. You receive the official search report. 4. Lawyer interprets: clean, curable (arrears/consent obtainable), or fatal (competing title, reservation). Parallel track: the <strong>online portal (onlineservices.lc.gov.gh)</strong> for initiation and progress tracking - especially valuable for diaspora buyers.</p><h2>How do you read a bad report?</h2><p>Competing registered interest = walk away. Unpaid ground rent = price it in and clear before completion. Missing concurrence = curable only if the true custodian cooperates - verify identity first. Vague boundaries = licensed re-survey before anything else.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>GHS 400 search vs total loss: the cheapest insurance in the transaction.</li><li>Only ~10% of buyers search - join the 10%.</li><li>Report interpretation needs your lawyer, not the agent.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>How long does a search take?</strong><br>Days to weeks depending on region and records digitisation (GELIS expanding across 7+ regions). Start before price talks conclude.</p><p><strong>Can I search from abroad?</strong><br>Yes - portal plus lawyer. Never rely on screenshots from the seller.</p><p><strong>Does a clean search guarantee safety?</strong><br>It guarantees the registry position at search date. Register promptly after - delays reopen the window for competing filings.</p><p><em>Sources: Lands Commission online services; Africanvestor due-diligence guide 2026.</em></p><p><em>Buying land in Ghana? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> maps verified diaspora lawyers, surveyors and REAC-registered agents - diligence before deposits.</em></p>', 'The highest-ROI GHS 400 in Ghana real estate. What the search reveals, how to run it (in person + online portal), and how to read the report.', ARRAY['land','title search','Lands Commission','verification'], 'Land & Title', 'published', '2026-10-09T08:00:00.000Z', 'Lands Commission Title Search: GHS 400 Walkthrough', 'The GHS 400 check that prevents six-figure losses: how Ghana''s title search works, what the report reveals, and how to read it.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'lands-commission-title-search-ghana-walkthrough');
