SELECT 'escrow-ghana-property-transactions-guide', 'Escrow for Ghana Property: How to Never Pay a Seller Directly', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Route every significant property payment through your lawyer''s escrow (or bank escrow): funds release only when agreed conditions - clean search, executed indenture, concurrence, registration lodged - are met. Direct-to-seller payment is the mechanism of nearly every documented scam.</p><h2>How does escrow work in practice?</h2><p>You deposit into a <strong>neutral account</strong> (your lawyer''s client account or bank escrow). The agreement lists <strong>release conditions</strong>: verified title search, executed documents, required consents, registration filing receipts. The holder releases in tranches as each condition evidences. Seller gets paid; you get title - neither moves first unprotected.</p><h2>What conditions should you set?</h2><p>Deposit (5-10%) on signed agreement + clean search. Balance on executed indenture + concurrence + registration lodgement receipts. Retention (5-10%) until title certificate issues. Every condition needs a named evidence document and a deadline with refund triggers.</p><h2>What does it cost and who holds?</h2><p>Lawyer escrow typically folds into 1-2% legal fees; bank escrow charges schedule fees. Holder must be <strong>your</strong> counsel or a neutral institution - never the seller''s lawyer alone, never an agent, never family.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Escrow converts trust into procedure.</li><li>''Pay direct for a discount'' is the oldest discount in the scam book.</li><li>Refund triggers with dates beat promises every time.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Is escrow common in Ghana?</strong><br>Increasingly, via lawyers and banks - and its absence in a deal is itself a red flag.</p><p><strong>Can escrow hold documents too?</strong><br>Yes - originals lodge with the holder pending conditions, preventing parallel sales during your window.</p><p><strong>What if the seller refuses escrow?</strong><br>Decline the deal. Legitimate sellers prefer escrow; only scammers need your money unprotected.</p><p><em>Sources: Ghana Ground Up escrow explainer; Africanvestor payment guidance.</em></p><p><em>Buying land in Ghana? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> maps verified diaspora lawyers, surveyors and REAC-registered agents - diligence before deposits.</em></p>', 'Lawyer escrow vs personal accounts: how neutral third-party holding works in Ghana deals, what it costs, and release conditions that protect both sides.', ARRAY['land','escrow','payments','fraud'], 'Land & Title', 'published', '2026-10-09T08:00:00.000Z', 'Escrow for Ghana Property Transactions', 'Never pay a seller directly: how escrow works in Ghana property deals, release conditions, costs, and the red flags it filters automatically.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'escrow-ghana-property-transactions-guide');
