SELECT 'ghana-rent-act-tenant-rights-2026', 'Ghana Rent Act: Your Rights (6-Month Cap, Agreements, Refunds)', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Ghana''s Rent Act 1963 caps advance rent at 6 months (long tenancy) / 1 month (short), requires written tenancy agreements, and punishes violations with fines or jail. A new rent commissioner and taskforce promise enforcement - know the law before you negotiate.</p><h2>What exactly does the law cap?</h2><p><strong>Long tenancy: max 6 months advance. Short tenancy: max 1 month.</strong> Demanding 1-3 years is an offence. Landlords risk fines or up to two years'' imprisonment. Tenants who fail to demand written agreements also offend - paper protects both sides.</p><h2>How do you enforce your rights?</h2><p>1. Register the tenancy (rentcontrol.mwh.gov.gh within 14 days for rentals). 2. Report violations to the Rent Control Department / new taskforce rather than paying quietly. 3. Overbilling established? PURC-style precedent shows regulators can order refunds - documented overpayment is recoverable. 4. ~60% of tenancies lack agreements: being in the documented 40% is itself leverage.</p><h2>Why hasn''t the law worked until now?</h2><p>60 years without a substantive commissioner, weak department capacity, tenant fear of eviction, and scarcity that lets landlords dictate. The National Rental Assistance Scheme helped formal workers only. Enforcement plus supply is the fix analysts demand.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>6 months is the legal ceiling - anything above is negotiable illegality.</li><li>Written agreement first, money second, always.</li><li>Report; silence is what priced the trap.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Can a landlord evict me for insisting on 6 months?</strong><br>Retaliatory eviction for asserting statutory rights is challengeable - document everything and seek the Department.</p><p><strong>Do agent fees have caps?</strong><br>Customary ~10% of advance; fold it into your total-cost comparison between listings.</p><p><strong>Does the Act cover Airbnb/short-stays?</strong><br>Short tenancy rules apply; long-stay ''short-let'' arrangements to dodge caps are a grey zone - get advice.</p><p><em>Sources: Rent Act 1963; The Africa Report 2026; Rent Control Department.</em></p><p><em>House-hunting from abroad? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> connects you with diaspora homeowners and vetted agents who quote legal advances - not obroni prices.</em></p>', 'The 1963 Act caps advances at 6 months, criminalises overcharging, and now has a commissioner. The tenant-rights brief landlords hope you never read.', ARRAY['rent','Rent Act','rights','housing'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-13T08:00:00.000Z', 'Ghana Rent Act: Tenant Rights (2026)', 'The 6-month cap, mandatory agreements, and the new rent commissioner: the tenant-rights brief every Accra renter needs.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'ghana-rent-act-tenant-rights-2026');
