SELECT 'accra-flood-zones-where-not-to-buy', 'Accra Flood Zones: Where NOT to Buy Property', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Parts of Accra flood yearly - not from freak rain but from waterways, valleys and dam releases. Never buy without rainy-season visits, neighbour interviews, assembly planning confirmation and elevated finished-floor levels in your build spec.</p><h2>Which areas flood repeatedly?</h2><p>Known perennial zones include Kasoa corridors, lower McCarthy Hill, Weija downstream (dam-gate releases), Oblo, Ashaley Botwe lakefront sections and low-lying valleys across the metropolis. Builders keep selling; rains keep collecting. Treat any ''too cheap for the area'' plot as a flood suspect until proven otherwise.</p><h2>What is the buying protocol?</h2><p>1. Visit in peak rains - dry-season land lies. 2. Ask neighbours and shopkeepers, not agents. 3. Check assembly planning/flood records. 4. Surveyor confirms elevation, drainage paths, waterway setbacks. 5. Build spec: raised floors, drainage, waterproofing - or walk away.</p><h2>Valley, hill or flat - which is safest?</h2><p>Valleys flood; hilltops erode and lose road access in storms; flats need drainage proof. Each terrain taxes you differently - budget the mitigation or choose differently.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Recurrent flooding is a location feature, not bad luck.</li><li>Rainy-season diligence is non-negotiable.</li><li>Flood history should discount price - or disqualify the plot.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Can engineering fix a flood plot?</strong><br>Sometimes, at costs that erase the discount. Get the engineer''s quote before the purchase, not after.</p><p><strong>Does insurance cover flooding?</strong><br>Standard policies often exclude known flood zones - confirm coverage and premiums pre-purchase.</p><p><strong>Are new developments protected?</strong><br>Only if drainage infrastructure is delivered, not promised. Inspect in rain.</p><p><em>Sources: Africa Building Hub flood series; assembly planning records.</em></p><p><em>House-hunting from abroad? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> connects you with diaspora homeowners and vetted agents who quote legal advances - not obroni prices.</em></p>', 'Kasoa corridors, Weija downstream, waterways and valleys: Accra''s perennial flood map and the rainy-season buying protocol.', ARRAY['flooding','location','Accra','due diligence'], 'Land & Title', 'published', '2026-10-13T08:00:00.000Z', 'Accra Flood Zones: Where NOT to Buy', 'Yearly floods, bulldozers, trapped equity: Accra''s flood-zone map and the rainy-season protocol for safe buying.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'accra-flood-zones-where-not-to-buy');
