SELECT 'fintech-licence-ghana-bank-of-ghana-requirements', 'Fintech Licence in Ghana: Bank of Ghana Requirements Explained', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Ghana fintech needs general incorporation (2 directors) PLUS sector rules: minimum 3 directors, Bank of Ghana licence category with integrity capital, possible SEC overlap, and full AML/KYC systems. Start with a compliance audit mapping general + sector + conditional requirements before writing code.</p><h2>Who regulates your fintech?</h2><p>Primarily the <strong>Bank of Ghana</strong> (payment systems, e-money, FX); secondarily the <strong>SEC</strong> for investment-adjacent products. Licence categories set different integrity-capital floors - confirm your exact activity''s category before capital planning.</p><h2>What is the compliance stack?</h2><p>General: incorporation, directors (3 for fintech), secretary, auditor, GRA, SSNIT, assembly permits, office insurance. Sector: BoG licence application, fit-and-proper tests, systems audits, AML/CFT frameworks, reporting lines. Conditional: fire permits, data-protection registration, postal-commission rules for delivery arms.</p><h2>What kills fintech entrants?</h2><p>Building before licensing clarity (categories dictate architecture), underestimating integrity-capital lock-up, and ignoring tax from day one (''the taxman always comes - backdated''). Honest founder conversation early beats enforcement later.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Licence category first, product second.</li><li>Capital must be licensable, not just spendable.</li><li>Governance (3 directors, no director-secretary) is examined, not decorative.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Can foreigners own fintech 100%?</strong><br>Subject to GIPC minimums plus sector rules - counsel must confirm current category treatment.</p><p><strong>How long does licensing take?</strong><br>Months with complete dossiers; open-ended with gaps. Pre-application engagement shortens it.</p><p><strong>Sandbox options?</strong><br>Discuss regulatory sandbox/testing avenues with counsel - pathways evolve.</p><p><em>Sources: Raygan fintech counsel; Bank of Ghana payment-systems regime.</em></p><p><em>Structuring a Ghana venture? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> surfaces diaspora founders, lawyers and sector operators - diligence your plan against people who survived it.</em></p>', 'Integrity capital, 3 directors minimum, SEC overlap. What it really takes to launch fintech in Ghana - and the compliance audit to run first.', ARRAY['fintech','Bank of Ghana','licence','regulation'], 'Entrepreneurship', 'published', '2026-10-17T08:00:00.000Z', 'Fintech Licence in Ghana: BoG Requirements', 'Integrity capital, extra directors, SEC overlap: what launching fintech in Ghana really requires - starting with a compliance audit.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'fintech-licence-ghana-bank-of-ghana-requirements');
