SELECT 'diaspora-mortgages-ghana-compared-2026', 'Diaspora Mortgages in Ghana Compared (2026): 12% USD vs 25% Cedi', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Major banks (FNB, Stanbic, Republic) offer diaspora mortgages: ~20-30% deposit, foreign income documentation, ~12% USD-denominated vs ~25% cedi rates. Developer payment plans (30-50% upfront, 12-24 month spreads, often interest-free) frequently beat mortgages for eligible buyers.</p><h2>What do banks require?</h2><p>Proof of foreign income (contracts, payslips, tax returns, bank statements), valid ID, 20-30% deposit, property valuation, and patience - qualification mirrors home-country mortgage depth. USD loans kill exchange risk; cedi loans price it at ~25%.</p><h2>Mortgage vs developer plan - which wins?</h2><p><strong>Developer plan:</strong> no interest, simpler approval, shorter tenor - ideal if you can fund 30-50% upfront and clear within 1-2 years. <strong>Mortgage:</strong> longer tenor, interest cost, deeper diligence - suits steady earners buying completed stock. Off-plan + developer plan is the classic diaspora combo.</p><h2>What about remittance-based investing?</h2><p>Regular remitters can route into real-estate trust/fund products from reputable firms - turning consumption transfers into accumulating assets. Verify operator licensing and redemption terms identically to any investment.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>USD mortgages (~12%) beat cedi (~25%) for dollar earners.</li><li>Developer plans often cheaper than mortgages for the disciplined.</li><li>Deposit discipline (20-50%) decides your options - start saving before shopping.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Can I get pre-approval from abroad?</strong><br>Yes - banks process diaspora files remotely with complete documentation packs.</p><p><strong>Are rates fixed?</strong><br>Confirm fixation vs variability in writing - cedi volatility makes this decisive.</p><p><strong>What yields cover the mortgage?</strong><br>Prime long-let 7-9% gross rarely covers 12%+ fully - model net cash flow, not hope.</p><p><em>Sources: Ghana Ground Up S1E12; bank diaspora desks 2025-26.</em></p><p><em>Structuring a Ghana venture? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> surfaces diaspora founders, lawyers and sector operators - diligence your plan against people who survived it.</em></p>', 'FNB, Stanbic, Republic compared: 20-30% deposits, foreign income docs, USD vs cedi rates - and when developer plans beat mortgages.', ARRAY['mortgage','financing','banks','diaspora'], 'Investment', 'published', '2026-10-17T08:00:00.000Z', 'Diaspora Mortgages Compared (2026)', '20-30% down, foreign income docs, 12% USD vs 25% cedi: diaspora mortgages compared - plus when developer plans win.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'diaspora-mortgages-ghana-compared-2026');
