SELECT 'water-security-ghana-home-tanks-boreholes-costs', 'Water Security at Home in Ghana: Tanks, Boreholes & Trucked Water', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Assume intermittency: overhead poly-tank + booster pump as baseline, borehole where geology and budget allow, trucked water as backup with known vendors. Confirm flow history with neighbours before renting or buying - never trust the landlord''s ''water flows always''.</p><h2>What is the baseline setup?</h2><p><strong>Overhead tank (500-1000L+) + booster pump + automatic switch:</strong> stores flow when it comes, pressurises the house always. Size to household × days of autonomy you want. Elevate for gravity feed backup when power fails too.</p><h2>When does a borehole pay?</h2><p>Where municipal flow is chronically poor and geology permits: drilling + pump + filtration + tank. Upfront thousands of cedis; payback against years of trucked water plus autonomy value. Test yield and quality before committing - dry boreholes are expensive holes.</p><h2>How do you manage trucked water?</h2><p>Pre-vet 2 vendors (price, reliability, source hygiene), keep tank-access clear for hoses, and track per-litre cost - chronic trucking often justifies the borehole within 1-2 years.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Storage first, source second, trucking as insurance.</li><li>Neighbour testimony beats landlord promises.</li><li>Water autonomy raises rentability and resale.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Is trucked water safe?</strong><br>Source-dependent: know your vendor''s source; filter + treat drinking water regardless.</p><p><strong>Can estates solve this?</strong><br>Managed developments with boreholes + treatment are a genuine premium worth paying for absentees.</p><p><strong>Why bills without water?</strong><br>Fixed charges + estimated billing persist through dry spells - dispute with logged outage evidence via PURC channels.</p><p><em>Sources: Returnee accounts; PURC consumer proceedings 2026.</em></p><p><em>Costing your move? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> connects you with returnees living your target lifestyle - real budgets, real streets, before you commit.</em></p>', 'Taps dry, bills wet. Poly-tanks, booster pumps, borehole economics and trucked-water math - the home water system that never leaves you dry.', ARRAY['water','borehole','tanks','utilities'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-21T08:00:00.000Z', 'Home Water Security in Ghana', 'Dry taps, wet bills: tanks, boosters, boreholes and trucked-water math - build the home system that never leaves you dry.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'water-security-ghana-home-tanks-boreholes-costs');
