SELECT 'internet-remote-workers-ghana-fibre-dual-sim-stack', 'Internet for Remote Workers in Ghana: The Fibre + Dual-SIM Stack', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> One connection is unemployment risk. Stack: home fibre (Surfline-type GHS 300-800) + MTN and Telecel SIMs + router UPS + phone-tethering readiness + 2 mapped cowork fallbacks. Schedule deep work for reliable windows; save continuously to cloud.</p><h2>Why is redundancy mandatory?</h2><p>MTN''s ~81% share means ''alternative networks'' often share fate; 11-99 fibre cuts daily; power takes routers down with it. Each layer fails independently - the stack survives what any single link doesn''t.</p><h2>What does the stack cost?</h2><p>Fibre GHS 300-800/month by speed; mobile data top-ups; a router UPS (hundreds of cedis, pays for itself in one saved deadline); cowork day-passes as insurance. Remote workers report ~GHS 500 all-in connectivity - trivial against one lost client.</p><h2>How do you work through dumsor?</h2><p>UPS bridges short cuts; charged laptop + tethered phone (towers often have backup) covers medium ones; generator-equipped coworks cover long ones. Keep an offline task queue for dead zones - dumsor can be productive with planning.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Two ISPs minimum, three paths preferred.</li><li>Router UPS is the highest-ROI gadget in the house.</li><li>Know your cowork backups before you need them.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Is Starlink an option?</strong><br>Evaluate current licensing/availability at purchase time - rules and resellers shift; verify legality before importing kits.</p><p><strong>Which mobile network first?</strong><br>MTN for coverage depth, Telecel second for failover - test both at your exact address.</p><p><strong>How much speed do I need?</strong><br>Video-call reliability matters more than headline Mbps - test sustained calls at your hours.</p><p><em>Sources: High Street Business 2026; remote-worker playbooks.</em></p><p><em>Costing your move? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> connects you with returnees living your target lifestyle - real budgets, real streets, before you commit.</em></p>', '81% MTN, fibre cuts daily, ~40% levies. The redundancy stack - fibre, two SIMs, router UPS, cowork backups - that keeps income online.', ARRAY['internet','remote work','MTN','connectivity'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-21T08:00:00.000Z', 'Internet Stack for Remote Workers', 'Fibre + dual-SIM + UPS + cowork backups: the redundancy stack keeping remote income online through cuts and dumsor.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'internet-remote-workers-ghana-fibre-dual-sim-stack');
