SELECT 'best-private-hospitals-accra-2026-compared', 'Best Private Hospitals in Accra (2026): Costs, Strengths & When to Go Public', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Use private hospitals (Nyaho, Lister, UGMC, Bloom) for speed, specialists and emergencies; public teaching hospitals (Korle-Bu) for complex specialty depth at lower cost. Expect ~GHS 50 registration, ~GHS 200-300 consults, plus meds/tests - carry insurance or a medical buffer always.</p><h2>How do the top privates compare?</h2><p><strong>Nyaho Medical Centre:</strong> premium diagnostics + specialists, higher bills. <strong>Lister Hospital:</strong> strong all-round private care. <strong>UG Medical Centre:</strong> university-backed, GHS ~50 registration + ~GHS 200 consults, good value with some waiting. <strong>Bloom (Airport):</strong> in-and-out speed at ~GHS 300/visit - full episodes can hit £70+. <strong>Korle-Bu Teaching:</strong> unmatched specialty depth for referrals, public-system trade-offs in comfort/speed.</p><h2>When does public care win?</h2><p>Minor ailments, vaccinations, and referred specialty procedures at teaching hospitals - costs stay low and expertise concentrates there. Pair public for basics with private for urgency: the standard returnee hybrid.</p><h2>What insurance covers what?</h2><p>NHIS: basics + referred secondary care. Private plans: premium hospitals, faster access, broader formularies. International: travel + home-country continuity. Serious conditions demand private/international - size cover to catastrophe, not colds.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Map your hospitals before illness, not during.</li><li>Hybrid public-private is the cost-effective default.</li><li>Keep records portable across facilities.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Which hospital for emergencies?</strong><br>Nearest quality private ER by night; teaching hospital by referral complexity. Pre-drive both routes.</p><p><strong>Are private hospitals overpriced?</strong><br>Versus public, yes; versus medical evacuation, no. Insurance arbitrages the gap.</p><p><strong>Do hospitals accept NHIS?</strong><br>Many for covered services - confirm your facility''s NHIS desk before relying on it.</p><p><em>Sources: Malaika in GH; Diaspora Affairs GH healthcare guides.</em></p><p><em>Moving with family? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> finds diaspora parents at your shortlisted schools and doctors returnees actually use - real experience before you commit.</em></p>', 'Nyaho, Lister, UGMC and Korle-Bu compared: registration, consult fees, strengths - plus when public care wins and the insurance that covers both.', ARRAY['healthcare','hospitals','Accra','insurance'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-25T08:00:00.000Z', 'Best Private Hospitals in Accra (2026)', 'Nyaho vs Lister vs UGMC vs Korle-Bu: fees, strengths, and when public care wins - the returnee hospital guide.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'best-private-hospitals-accra-2026-compared');
