SELECT 'nhis-enrolment-diaspora-guide-eligibility-process', 'NHIS Enrolment for Diasporans: Eligibility, Process & Limits', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Most resident foreigners can join Ghana''s NHIS for basic consultations, essential meds and referred secondary care - but 75% of immigrants never enrol, deterred by paper processes. Register at district offices with ID + photos + premium; keep private cover for premium/specialist care.</p><h2>Who is eligible?</h2><p>Legal residents including qualifying foreigners - yet awareness and analog enrolment suppress uptake (2026 study: 75% of immigrants never enrolled vs 7.8% of locals). Employer/university-linked signups are the easiest on-ramp; self-enrolment at NHIS district offices works with passport/permit + photos + premium payment.</p><h2>What does NHIS actually cover?</h2><p>Outpatient consultations, essential drug list meds, maternity basics, emergencies at accredited facilities, and referred secondary care. Exclusions: most premium private care, advanced imaging abroad-style, non-essential drugs. The 2026 Free Primary Healthcare layer adds preventive/basic access regardless of enrolment - secondary care still keys off NHIS.</p><h2>Why keep private cover too?</h2><p>Speed, choice of facility, specialist depth, and meds outside the essential list. A third of insured immigrants already use private schemes - the de facto two-tier reality. Size private cover to your risk: catastrophe-first.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Eligible ≠ enrolled - close the gap in week one.</li><li>NHIS for base, private for peak.</li><li>Keep cards + digital copies on every phone.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>How much is the premium?</strong><br>Income-banded, modest annually - confirm current bands at enrolment; informal-sector flat rates apply to many.</p><p><strong>How long is the card valid?</strong><br>Annual renewal - diary it; lapsed cards fail at the worst moments.</p><p><strong>Can visitors enrol?</strong><br>Short-stay visitors generally can''t - travel insurance covers visits; NHIS covers residence.</p><p><em>Sources: 2026 NHIS-access study; NHIA; Free Primary Healthcare policy briefs.</em></p><p><em>Moving with family? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> finds diaspora parents at your shortlisted schools and doctors returnees actually use - real experience before you commit.</em></p>', '75% of immigrants never enrol. Who qualifies, how to register, what it covers - and why private cover still matters on top.', ARRAY['NHIS','insurance','healthcare','eligibility'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-25T08:00:00.000Z', 'NHIS Enrolment for Diasporans: Guide', '75% of immigrants never enrol in NHIS. Eligibility, registration, coverage - and why private cover still sits on top.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'nhis-enrolment-diaspora-guide-eligibility-process');
