SELECT 'international-schools-accra-fees-admissions-2026', 'International Schools in Accra (2026): Fees, Waitlists & Admissions Timeline', '<p class="tldr"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Top Accra international schools run GHS 8,000-50,000 per term with peak-season waitlists. Start 9+ months out: shortlist 3-4, assess, apply broadly, confirm before shipping. Fees + transport + activities define the true education budget.</p><h2>Which schools lead and what do they cost?</h2><p>Ghana International School (GIS), SOS Hermann Gmeiner, Tema International (TIS), Delhi Public (DPS), Al Rayan, Morgan International, Roman Ridge, Lincoln Community (premium US-curriculum apex). Terms span ~GHS 8K-50K by tier - plus admission fees, transport, meals, activities. A £400/term mid-tier vs £65/day UK underlines the value - when you hold the seat.</p><h2>What is the admissions timeline?</h2><p><strong>T-9mo:</strong> shortlist by curriculum (British, IB, American, hybrid) + visit/test windows. <strong>T-6mo:</strong> assessments + applications to 3-4 schools. <strong>T-3mo:</strong> acceptances, deposits, transport routing. <strong>T-0:</strong> orientation + records transfer. Peak (August/September) competition is fiercest - January entries breathe easier.</p><h2>How do you choose curriculum?</h2><p>Match exit plans: UK-university-bound → British; US-bound → American/Lincoln; undecided/global → IB. Switching systems mid-stream costs adaptation - decide on destination, not prestige.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>Seats are the scarce good; fees are just the price.</li><li>Apply to 3-4; acceptances are not guaranteed.</li><li>True cost = fees + transport + activities + deposits.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><strong>Are local private schools viable?</strong><br>Yes - strong Ghanaian private schools at lower fees suit many families; assess outcomes, not labels.</p><p><strong>Do schools offer diaspora support?</strong><br>Top ones run orientation + buddy systems - ask admissions specifically.</p><p><strong>What records transfer?</strong><br>Reports, immunisation, assessments - apostilled/translated where required. Start early.</p><p><em>Sources: Accra Street Journal 2025; parent accounts; school publications.</em></p><p><em>Moving with family? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> finds diaspora parents at your shortlisted schools and doctors returnees actually use - real experience before you commit.</em></p>', 'GIS to Lincoln: GHS 8-50K terms, peak-season waitlists, and the 9-month admissions timeline that secures seats.', ARRAY['schools','education','fees','admissions','family'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-25T08:00:00.000Z', 'International Schools in Accra (2026)', 'Fees, waitlists and the 9-month timeline: securing international school seats in Accra without panic.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'international-schools-accra-fees-admissions-2026');
